SUMMARY:Maxwell\, Pressley Cove(s) loop
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nNOTE: i went ahead and switched th
 is hike to Sunday 03 May at 10 due to weather concerns\n\nthis is about a 
 5 mile (maybe a bit less) loop with 1000-ish feet of elevation gain in the
  ranger station section of Pisgah.\n\nthe starting point is the newer grav
 el parking lot near Avery creek about 1.6 miles in on the forest service r
 oad leading to the stables\, Twin Falls etc. just past the Bennett Gap tra
 il. carpooling is encouraged\n\nfrom the starting point\, ascent to Maxwel
 l Cove is via an unmarked trail further down the road\, with an approx 1 m
 ile climb. We then wend our way up Maxwell\, past an interesting historica
 l ruin to Pressley Gap\, where the Black Mountain trail crosses. Then back
  down Maxwell to Pressley Cove trail\, which leads back down to the parkin
 g area.\n\nwell behaved dogs are welcome on this hike\n\nsay 2 - 2.5 mph p
 ace\n\ngear up as appropriate\, trekking poles are an option. bring a snac
 k as we'll take a break mid-hike. and plenty of water\n\nground rules:\n\n
 if you sign up\, show up or change your status. a no-show may undercut a m
 otivated wait-lister. (repeated no-shows will have consequences) likewise\
 , if you're on the wait list at the time of the hike\, don't presume to ju
 st show up\n\n2 ) be sure you are in adequate physical shape to complete t
 he event\n\n1. show consideration. emphasize group effort and group cohesi
 on. I hike for stress reduction and want to keep it that way.\n\nLEGALESE\
 nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transp
 ortation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for the
 ir own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical 
 conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to onese
 lf and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group ca
 n assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. By signing up for this event
 \, participant understands and agrees
