SUMMARY:Blue Ridge Parkway Walkers Knob Overlook to Cane Gap. Out/Back FIT
 NESS HIKE.
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n\\*\\*\\*!!!\\*\\*\\*Hike directio
 n has changed since first posting on Friday. Reread the instructions as we
  are starting at Walkers Knob Overlook off BPR.\n\n**It is an honor to be 
 selected to lead this hike...thank you Allen for your confidence in me. I 
 hope we don't end up in Tennessee\, or Oklahoma\, or something.**\n\n**Sig
 n up begins 6am on Sunday**\n\n**MEETUP OPTION:**\n**Carpool option 1:** M
 eet at **8:45 am**\, at the Folk Art Center to follow or carpool.\n**Carpo
 ol option 2:** Meet at Weaverville Ingles (across from Publix) near gas pu
 mps at **8:35am**. We will travel up Ox Creek to BPR so you could also mee
 t us there if easier(approx 8:55am).\n\nPease post if you plan to carpool 
 and where you will join the caravan\, otherwise see you at the TH at 9:30 
 am. Walkers Knob Overlook Trailhead is approximately 40 minutes from Folk 
 Art Center and 45-50 minutes from Ingles Weaverville.\n\n**HIKE DESCRIPTIO
 N\;**\nTwo options: The primary option is a back country STRENUOUS approx 
 12 mile O&B hike passing Point Misery\, Little Butt\, and Big Butt and con
 tinues to Cane Gap where we will turn around. Lunch at either Big Butt or 
 Little Butt on the return. The alternate option is to stop at Big Butt on 
 the outward hike and turn around. This option chops off about 2 miles and 
 1000ft elevation.\n\nThere are over 350 well-crafted wooden steps ( out an
 d back) on a trail which is mostly under a deciduous forest. The trail is 
 maintained by the NC High Peaks Association. T**he elevation gain estimate
 s (primary option) is approximately +/-3\,300 feet\, level 10\\*.** High M
 ountain Temperatures on this hike are tipically 10+ degrees cooler than As
 heville.\n\n**PACE:** Fitness hikes proceed at a steady pace averaging 2.5
  MPH on climbs and/or rugged trail conditions\, and 3+ MPH on level/downgr
 ade sections with brief regrouping at trail intersections\, or as needed. 
 There are plenty of cardiochallenges and endurance sections on this hike w
 hich is for conditioned hikers. Please know your hiking abilities before s
 igning on. Any questions please post on this meetuo site or message me.\n\
 n**Trailhead Directions**. Put Walkers Knob Overlook into Google or Apple 
 Maps. Big Butt Trail is adjacent to parking area.\n\nIf you sign up for th
 is hike or waitlist and change your mind go back to the RSVP link and canc
 el your reservation to free the space for other hikers.\n\n**Weather: Canc
 ellation** and / rescheduling will be made on or before 7 AM hike day if i
 nclimate weather forecasts indicates potential unsuitable conditions.\n\n*
 *DOGS:** Trail-friendly dogs welcome\n\n**\\*HIKE LEVELS**...are based on 
 the total elevation gain (or estimates).\nLevel (1) Up to 600 feet of elev
 ation gain.\nLevel (2) 600'- 900'\; Level (3) 900' - 1200'\; Level (4) 120
 0' - 1500'\; Level (5) 1\,500' - 1\,800'\; Level (6) 1\,800' - 2\,100'\; L
 evel (7)\\* 2\,100' - 2\,400'\; Level (8) 2\,400' - 2700'\; Level (9) 2700
 ' - 3000' **Level (10) 3000' - 4000'\;**\n\n**Release of Liability:**\nThe
  organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The f
 unction of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or 
 participate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily 
 agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising fr
 om\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. In addition\, you ac
 knowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/term
 s](https://www.meetup.com/terms)\n\nULTIMATE HIKES are 4000+ feet elevatio
 n gain. I
